  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Saran G vs Dr.Rajan.N.Khobragade Ias on 11 February, 2020 Author: S.Manikumar Bench: S.Manikumar, Shaji P.Chaly In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable The Chief Justice Mr.S.Manikumar & The Honourable Mr. Justice Shaji P.Chaly Tuesday, The 11Th Day Of February 2020 / 22Nd Magha, 1941 Con.Case(C).No.2139 Of 2019 In Op(Kat). 342/2018 Against The Judgment In Op(Kat) 342/2018 Of High Court Of Kerala Petitioners/Petitioners In Op(Kat): 1 Saran G., Aged 46 Years S/O.Gopalan, Evaluation Assistant (Junior Health Inspector Grade I), Health Information Cell, Directorate Of Health Services, Thiruvananthapuram - 695 035. 2 Jyothi Sabu G., Aged 49 Years S/O.Gopalakrishnan Nair, Junior Health Inspector Grade-I, Chc Ezhumattoor, Pathanamthitta - 689 586. By Advs. Sri.P.Nandakumar Sri.S.Aneesh Smt.Amrutha Sanjeev Respondents/Respondents No.2 To 4 In O.P.(Kat): 1 Dr.Rajan.N.Khobragade Ias, Age And Father'S Name Not Known To The Petitioner, Secretary To Government Of Kerala, Health And Family Welfare Department, Government Secretariat, Thiruvananthapuram - 695 001. 2 Dr.Sarita R.L., Age And Father'S Name Not Known To The Petitioner, Director Of Health Services, Office Of The Directorate Of Health Services, Thiruvananthapuram - 695 035. 3 Dr.Rathan U.Kelkar, Ias, Age And Fathers Name Not Known To The Petitioner, Food Safety Commissioner, Food Safety Saran G vs Dr.Rajan.N.Khobragade Ias on 11 February, 2020 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/175661523/ 1 Commissionerate, Thycaud, Thiruvananthapuram - 695 014. Other Present: Sr Gp Sri.Tek Chand For Respondents This Contempt Of Court Case (Civil) Having Come Up For Admission On 11.02.2020, The Court On The Same Day Delivered The Following: Con.Case(C).No.2139 Of 2019 2 Judgment",
    "facts": "The impugned order of the Tribunal in so far as it relates to the petitioners shall stand modified and necessary follow up action shall be taken by the respondents forthwith.\" 2. Alleging wilful disobedience, instant contempt application has been filed. 3. On 6.2.2020, Mr.Tek Chand, learned Government Pleader who took notice on behalf of the respondents submitted that promotion order has already been prepared however the concerned officer was not in station to issue the order. A copy of the said G.O. is extracted hereunder: \"The Hon'ble High Court in the judgment read as 1st paper above has directed that all vacancies of Food Inspectors (approximately five in number) that existed up to the date of coming into force of the Food Safety and Standards Rules, 2011 on 5.8.2011 Saran G vs Dr.Rajan.N.Khobragade Ias on 11 February, 2020 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/175661523/ 2 should be filled up by qualified Junior Health Inspectors. The Junior Health Inspectors shall be promoted to the re-designated post of Food Safety Officer by the appointing authority under the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. The remaining substantive vacancies to the post of Food Safety Officer shall be filled up from the ranked list published by the Public Service Commission on 9.9.2016. 2. As per Government order read as 2nd paper above, Government had directed Director of Health Services to prepare and furnish a proposal in respect of the qualified Junior Health Inspectors fit for promotion to the post of Food Inspectors based on their seniority and qualification in accordance with the judgment read as Ist paper above. 3. Accordingly, as per order read as 4th paper above, Director of Health Services prepared and published the finalized list of departmental candidates fit for promotion to Con.Case(C).No.2139 OF 2019 the post of Food Inspector (Re-designated as Food Safety Officer). As per letter read as 5th paper above, Director of Health Services has reported that as per order read as 3rd paper above Junior Health Inspectors with regular service of 5 years can be considered only in the absence of Health Inspectors. Out of the 198 applications received there are many applicants who held the Post of Health Inspectors before 05/08/2011. Hence the Director of Health Services has prepared the list of departmental candidates fit for promotion to the post of Food inspectors including 8 senior most candidates who were Health Inspectors before 05/08/2011 fit for promotion to the post of Food Inspector (Re-designated as Food Safety Officer), before Government. Government have examined the matter in detail and pleased to promote the following senior most 4 candidates, from the list of departmental candidates fit for promotion to the post of Food Inspector (Re- designated as Food Safety Officer) as Food Inspectors (re-designated as Food Safety Officers) and to absorb them in Food Safety Department from the Department of Health Services, as per the existing rules. Director of Health Services shall take necessary steps to relieve the Officers in time. The Officers shall report before Commissioner of Food Safety immediately after relieving from Health Services Department.",
    "arguments": "5. Smt.Amrutha Sanjeev, learned counsel for the contempt petitioners has submitted that the orders have not been implemented in letter and spirit.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "5. Smt.Amrutha Sanjeev, learned counsel for the contempt petitioners has submitted that the orders have not been implemented in letter and spirit.",
